  [1;34mMR101 · create-index-non-concurrent[m

  [1mWhat it detects[m

  [35mCREATE[m [35mINDEX[m or [35mCREATE[m [35mUNIQUE[m [35mINDEX[m without [35mCONCURRENTLY[m on a table that this change set didn't
  create.

  [1mWhy it's dangerous[m

  Building an index reads the whole table. Without [35mCONCURRENTLY[m, Postgres holds a [35mSHARE[m lock on the
  table for the entire build. Reads still work, but every [35mINSERT[m, [35mUPDATE[m and [35mDELETE[m waits. On a
  table with millions of rows the build can take minutes, and the application's write requests queue
  up behind it.

  [1mLock & impact[m

  [90mStatement:[m [35mCREATE[m [35mINDEX[m
  [90mLock:[m [35mSHARE[m
  [90mBlocks:[m [35mINSERT[m, [35mUPDATE[m, [35mDELETE[m
  [90mWork:[m full table scan and index build

  [90mStatement:[m [35mCREATE[m [35mINDEX[m [35mCONCURRENTLY[m
  [90mLock:[m [35mSHARE[m [35mUPDATE[m [35mEXCLUSIVE[m
  [90mBlocks:[m other schema changes and [35mVACUUM[m
  [90mWork:[m two table scans, waits for older transactions

  These locks apply to PostgreSQL 12 through 18.

  [1mHow to fix[m

  Add [35mCONCURRENTLY[m and run the statement outside a transaction. Postgres rejects [35mCREATE[m [35mINDEX[m
  [35mCONCURRENTLY[m inside a transaction block, so turn off the migration tool's transaction for this
  migration.

    [35mCREATE[m [35mINDEX[m [35mCONCURRENTLY[m idx_orders_status [35mON[m orders (status);

  If a concurrent build fails, it leaves an [35mINVALID[m index behind. Drop it with [35mDROP[m [35mINDEX[m
  [35mCONCURRENTLY[m and run the migration again.

  [1mWhen it's safe to ignore[m

  [90m•  [mThe table is empty or very small in every environment.
  [90m•  [mThe migration runs during a maintenance window with writes stopped.
  [90m•  [mThe table is partitioned. Postgres can't build an index on a partitioned table concurrently.
     Create the index concurrently on each partition, then create it on the parent with [35mON[m [35mONLY[m and
     attach the partition indexes.

  [1mExamples[m

  Bad:

    [35mCREATE[m [35mINDEX[m idx_orders_status [35mON[m orders (status);

  Good:

    [35mCREATE[m [35mINDEX[m [35mCONCURRENTLY[m idx_orders_status [35mON[m orders (status);

  [1mReferences[m

  [90m•  [m[34mPostgreSQL:[m [34mBuilding[m [34mindexes[m [34mconcurrently[m
     [34m(https://www.postgresql.org/docs/current/sql-createindex.html#SQL-CREATEINDEX-CONCURRENTLY)[m
  [90m•  [m[34mPostgreSQL:[m [34mTable-level[m [34mlock[m [34mmodes[m
     [34m(https://www.postgresql.org/docs/current/explicit-locking.html#LOCKING-TABLES)[m
